<title>UK: SmithKline says sales drop at DPS division.</title>
<headline>SmithKline says sales drop at DPS division.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK drugs group SmithKline Beecham said on Tuesday first quarter revenues at its Diversified Pharmaceutical Services division fell 64 percent to 41 million stg.</p>
<p>The fall primarily stemmed from a change in the way it sells its services, converting from annual contracts with individuals and companies to a pay-per-use system, SmithKline said.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
